  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "Patrician house (3×3, D-054; tier language: dressed stone, ornament, towers — still warm): three storeys on a paved plot — a dressed warm-stone ground floor with an arched door, two plastered upper floors (the first jettied) between pale stone string courses, glazed windows with sills, a hipped terracotta roof. v0 a square tower at the back right rising a storey above the roof under a pyramid roof with a brass finial; v1 a loggia (columned arcade with a balustraded terrace and planters) in front of a wider ochre house; v2 a round corner turret on corbels with a conical roof and an oriel on a mirrored house.",
